1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,643
Drinking iced water...

2
00:00:01,643 --> 00:00:02,786
makes you fat?

3
00:00:02,786 --> 00:00:03,670
Myth...

4
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:04,558
or fact?

5
00:00:05,732 --> 00:00:06,924
The answer...

6
00:00:06,924 --> 00:00:07,791
MYTH!

7
00:00:07,791 --> 00:00:08,371
Iced water has

8
00:00:08,371 --> 00:00:09,371
zero calories!

9
00:00:09,371 --> 00:00:11,567
But there's a real culprit...

10
00:00:11,567 --> 00:00:12,449
at the end of the video.

11
00:00:12,449 --> 00:00:13,104
In fact, it's the opposite:

12
00:00:13,104 --> 00:00:15,485
iced water is about four degrees.

13
00:00:15,485 --> 00:00:17,010
Your body has to warm it

14
00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:18,654
up to thirty-seven degrees.

15
00:00:18,654 --> 00:00:19,664
That takes energy:

16
00:00:19,664 --> 00:00:20,959
about sixteen calories

17
00:00:20,959 --> 00:00:22,191
per half liter!

18
00:00:22,191 --> 00:00:23,263
Tiny, sure,

19
00:00:23,263 --> 00:00:25,038
but it clearly won't make you fat.

20
00:00:25,376 --> 00:00:27,519
So, who's the culprit?

21
00:00:27,519 --> 00:00:28,180
SUGAR!

22
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:29,792
Plain iced water: zero calories.

23
00:00:29,792 --> 00:00:31,176
Sweet iced tea with two spoons of sugar:

24
00:00:31,176 --> 00:00:32,792
about a hundred calories!

25
00:00:32,792 --> 00:00:34,337
And the daily sugar limit

26
00:00:34,337 --> 00:00:35,856
is just four tablespoons.

27
00:00:35,856 --> 00:00:37,453
So, iced water?

28
00:00:37,453 --> 00:00:38,863
Safe, as long as it's plain!

29
00:00:38,863 --> 00:00:39,585
Send this to a friend

30
00:00:39,585 --> 00:00:42,091
who's still scared of ice!

